---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { site } from "../site";
import { url } from "../lib/url";
const { links } = site;
---

<Base title="About">
  <section class="wrap page prose">
    <h1>About</h1>
    <p>{site.intro}</p>

    <h2>How I build</h2>
    <p>
      I build with AI coding agents, mainly Anthropic's Claude Code. Each course project follows the same loop: read the
      specification, write a plan, implement it in small steps, audit the result and test it, with the plan, decisions and
      test results kept in the repository. Nothing counts as done until it passes black-box tests that drive the system the
      way the course autograder does, over its TCP/JSON protocol. The course then checks that I understand the code: I
      repair deliberately broken copies of my own projects without AI tools.
    </p>
    <p>
      This website, its demos and the first drafts of its write-ups were also made with Claude Code. Each project page says
      how AI was used on that project.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <ul>
      {links.email && <li><a href={`mailto:${links.email}`}>{links.email}</a></li>}
      {links.github && <li><a href={links.github}>GitHub</a></li>}
      {links.linkedin && <li><a href={links.linkedin}>LinkedIn</a></li>}
      {links.cv && <li><a href={url(links.cv)}>CV (PDF)</a></li>}
      {!links.email && !links.github && !links.linkedin && !links.cv && (
        <li class="muted">TODO: add links in <code>src/site.ts</code>.</li>
      )}
    </ul>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .page { padding-top: 40px; }
</style>
